=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web page (web/src/features/trips/pages/TripListPage.tsx, 366 lines) is the multi-drive
"Trips" report. Data source: `useTrips({ vehicle_id, limit, offset, start, end }) → GET
/trips` returning `Trip[]`. SI display contract: `total_distance_m` (metres),
`total_energy_wh` (Wh), `total_duration_s` (seconds) are SI; the page converts distance
at the render boundary via `convertDistanceFromSI` + `useUnits`, formats energy through
`useUnits().formatEnergy` (unit-aware kWh/Wh/MWh), and costs through
`useFormatting().formatCurrency` ({symbol}{number}). Efficiency is derived inline:
`whPerKm = total_energy_wh / (total_distance_m/1000)`, scaled by `KM_PER_MILE`
(1.609344) for imperial, labelled `Wh/mi` | `Wh/km`.

Parity manifest record (34 = 7 panels + 2 charts + 3 states + 22 strings):
  panels  : Total-Distance, Energy-Used, Total-Cost, Total-Trips (4× MetricCard),
            Top-Trips-by-Distance (ChartContainer), GlassPanel6 (All-Trips list),
            GlassPanel7 (per-trip TripRow)
  charts  : ChartContainer, BarChart      maps : 0
  states  : loading, empty, success
  strings : 22 bare trips.* keys (web key names)

Region map (web → native):
  • 4× <MetricCard label value icon color subtitle>  → statsGrid (shared MetricCard, P3)
  • <ChartContainer title ariaLabel … action={CSV/JSON}> + Recharts <BarChart
    layout="vertical"> (top-10 by distance) → TripListChartPanel + TripDistanceBarChart
    (Swift Charts BarMark, horizontal; longest bar on top)
  • <GlassPanel> "All Trips" wrapping the row list → tripListPanel (GlassPanel6)
  • <TripRow> (itself a <GlassPanel>) → TripListRow (GlassPanel7)
  • web Pagination/RangePicker/VehicleSelect/SavedViewMenu header actions are NOT manifest
    parity items for this unit; the query seam carries the same params (vehicle_id/limit/
    offset/start/end) so they bind when the host wires them.

PREDECESSOR / COLLISION FINDING (binding for the whole implementation):
  A sibling Trips port already exists at apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/TripsReplay*
  (the single-drive replay) with PUBLIC symbols TripsReplayPage/Model/…; the dashboard
  bundle owns TripSummary* (TripSummaryWidget/Row/Projection/DTO). Both compile into the
  SINGLE TeslaSync module (project.yml), and Swift forbids (a) two same-name types and
  (b) two same-basename files in one target. Pre-grep confirmed ZERO existing
  TripList*/TripListItem symbols and ZERO TripList* file basenames. Resolution: every
  type + file in this unit is `TripList…`-prefixed (value type `TripListItem`, not the
  taken `TripSummary`) and the shared P2 tokens / P3 components (MetricCard, GlassPanel,
  EmptyState, Skeleton, FadeIn, Swift Charts) / P1 Units facade are REUSED (DRY), not
  duplicated. The unit lives in the prescribed directory apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/.

STRING-CATALOG FINDING:
  Localizable.xcstrings carried only `translation.trips.*` (web-import namespace), not the
  bare keys the SwiftUI views resolve (the same convention the sibling uses). The 22 bare
  `trips.*` keys were added with the verbatim web English defaults (en) taken from
  web/src/i18n/en.json + the source `t(key, default)` fallbacks; the five count keys use
  `%lld` (`trips.stats.tripCount/driveCount/totalDrives`, `trips.row.drives/charges`).
  `trips.chart.title.aria` has no en.json entry (web uses the inline default) — added
  verbatim. JSON re-validated (12034 → 12056 keys).

DECISION — export actions (web CSV/JSON download buttons):
  The web ChartContainer `action` slot renders two ghost Buttons that download
  teslasync-trips-v2.csv / teslasync-trips.json. The HIG-native peer is `ShareLink`,
  which hands the serialized content to the system share sheet (Save to Files / AirDrop /
  …). The model serializes the CSV (id/name/dates/SI distance+energy/cost/counts, header
  first, RFC-4180-quoted) and the JSON (snake_case `Trip` array, SI verbatim) exactly like
  the web `handleExportCSV`/`exportAsJSON`. The two `trips.export.csv`/`trips.export.json`
  labels are the counted parity items; the ShareLinks always render (disabled when empty).

DECISION — "In progress" duration sentinel:
  Web `formatDuration` returns the literal 'In progress' for an open trip. To honor the
  zero-hardcoded-literal rule it resolves from the already-shipped catalog key
  `driveDetail.inProgress` ("In progress") — no new literal, no extra manifest key.

=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/   (8 files, 1296 lines)
  TripListModels.swift            TripListItem (SI) + TripListState + TripListDataSource + TripListQuery
  TripListStrings.swift           the 22 web keys (LocalizedStringKey/String) + count formatters + rawKeys
  TripListFormat.swift            date / duration / distance(SI→display) / energy / currency / efficiency
  TripListSampleData.swift        Sample (success) + Empty (empty) + Failing (error) data sources
  TripListPageModel.swift         @Observable model: load/refresh; totals + top-10 chart slice + CSV/JSON
  TripListCharts.swift            TripDistanceBarChart (Swift Charts) + TripListChartPanel (ChartContainer)
  TripListPage.swift              adaptive scaffold + 4 MetricCards + chart + All-Trips list + TripListRow + skeleton
  TripListRouteRegistration.swift NavigationDestination + /trips deep-link parser

Design notes:
  - @Observable `TripListPageModel` consumes a KMP-bindable data-source seam (`loadTrips`
    ← useTrips / GET /trips?vehicle_id=&limit=&offset=&start=&end=); the view holds no
    networking (ADR-004). Derives totalDistanceM/totalEnergyWh/totalCost/totalDrives (web
    memos) + topTripsByDistance (web chartData sort+slice(0,10)) — all SI.
  - SI only on the model; conversion at the SwiftUI render boundary via `Units` (P1/S5) +
    `@Environment(\.tsUnits)` (ADR-005). Distance metres→user unit + fmtInt + unit suffix;
    energy unit-aware via Units.formatEnergy; cost via CurrencyFormatting {symbol}{number};
    efficiency Wh/km derived from SI, ×KM_PER_MILE for imperial — nothing non-SI stored.
  - Adaptive macOS + iOS: ScrollView, 1100pt max content width, LazyVGrid stat cards reflow
    1→2→4 cols (.adaptive(minimum:220)), TripListRow uses ViewThatFits (HStack regular /
    VStack compact); `.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.large)` iOS-gated; one adaptive
    SwiftUI source (ADR-002/006).
  - Charts: native Swift Charts BarMark (never a WKWebView), horizontal (web layout=
    "vertical"), reversed categorical y-domain so the longest trip is on top, accent
    gradient, value+category axes tokenized, chart a11y label/value.
  - a11y: stat cards + chart + rows carry labels/traits; the list is a labelled container;
    each row combines children; dynamic Color.TS (light/dark/contrast), Dynamic Type via
    Font.TS, ≥44pt tap targets; export ShareLinks labelled.
  - Data source is a one-shot fetch (web useTrips has no live SSE subscription) — no
    >2-min staleness indicator is required for this unit (ADR-013 N/A here).
  - No #Preview blocks authored (this SDK's #Preview macro is ambiguous between SwiftUI and
    AppKit/UIKit, the documented baseline breakage) — keeps the unit clean-compiling; the
    Empty/Failing seams remain for the P9 XCTest phase.

